From: Ben Klopfenstein <benklop@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] video: ignore SDL_VIDEODRIVER values naming an unknown driver

SDL_VIDEODRIVER is read by both SDL 1.2 and SDL 2. Calculinux exports
SDL_VIDEODRIVER=kmsdrm for SDL 2 (sdl2-defaults.sh), which names no SDL 1.2
driver, so every SDL 1.2 app started from a login shell failed with "No
available video device" unless it overrode the variable.

When the named driver doesn't exist in this build, pick one automatically
as if the variable was unset. Naming an existing driver that turns out to
be unavailable still fails as before.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Calculinux-specific; SDL 1.2 is unmaintained]

diff --git a/src/video/SDL_video.c b/src/video/SDL_video.c
index 46285c9..9ce7e3a 100644
--- a/src/video/SDL_video.c
+++ b/src/video/SDL_video.c
@@ -188,7 +188,21 @@ int SDL_VideoInit (const char *driver_name, Uint32 flags)
 				}
 			}
 		}
-	} else {
+		/* SDL_VIDEODRIVER is shared with SDL 2, whose driver names
+		   ("kmsdrm", "wayland") mean nothing here. Don't let a value
+		   meant for SDL 2 keep every SDL 1.2 app from starting. */
+		if ( video == NULL ) {
+			for ( i=0; bootstrap[i]; ++i ) {
+				if ( SDL_strcasecmp(bootstrap[i]->name, driver_name) == 0) {
+					break;
+				}
+			}
+			if ( bootstrap[i] == NULL ) {
+				driver_name = NULL;
+			}
+		}
+	}
+	if ( driver_name == NULL ) {
 		for ( i=0; bootstrap[i]; ++i ) {
 			if ( bootstrap[i]->available() ) {
 				video = bootstrap[i]->create(index);
